-- Applied 2026-09-11 to CoA-Repack's acore_world. Re-apply after any fresh
-- acore_world import/rebuild -- see AGENTS.md's "Found (and fixed) while
-- testing bots" section for the full root-cause writeup. Regenerated by
-- reading the on-disk gtOCTRegenHP.dbc/gtRegenHPPerSpt.dbc/gtRegenMPPerSpt.dbc
-- files directly (single 4-byte float per record, "df" format, no id column)
-- and emitting REPLACE INTO rows for indices 1100-3199 (classes 12-32).
--
-- Extends the gt*regen*_dbc hotfix tables (acore_world) with rows for
-- Ascension's custom class ids 12-32, sourced from the on-disk .dbc files.
-- Without this, DBCStorageBase::LoadFromDB() replaces the file-loaded
-- 3200-row table with the DB table's 1100 rows, so any
-- OCTRegenHPPerSpirit()/OCTRegenMPPerSpirit() lookup for a custom class
-- indexes past row 1099 and returns null -> 0 regen.
--
-- CAVEAT (found on a later sweep, see AGENTS.md): the on-disk .dbc files
-- are NOT a byte-accurate match for CoA's live-tuned data -- cross-checking
-- against the untouched stock rows (0-1099) this script never modifies
-- found 100/1100, 100/1100, and 666/1100 mismatches respectively. The file
-- is some other dataset (different build/tuning pass), plausible-shaped but
-- not verified-correct. Still strictly better than the pre-fix state (zero
-- effective rows for classes 12-32), but a dev should eventually review the
-- exact per-level numbers rather than trust this as final tuning.

